WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.580
Hey guys, it's Jan here!
Wasn't it tough spotting the easter eggs for

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.490
The Good Dinosaur at the cinema?
But now it's out on DVD, I've been able to

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.280
find 8 Pixar and Disney easter eggs and references
you probably missed when you first saw the

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.059
movie.
If you noticed any others, I'd love to hear

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:19.560
about them in the comments below.
And of course, as this is an easter egg video,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.480
there will be some spoilers ahead if you haven't
seen the movie. So, if you're not ready for

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.660
that, check out my non-spoiler review of the
movie here.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.840
Let's kick off with a big Pixar regular! A-1-1-3,
was a quite hard one to find, but you can

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.940
spot it on the fence when Arlo goes to feed
the chickens.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.700
The A-1-1-3 easter egg has appeared in every
single Pixar movie to date and is a homage

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.150
to the classroom at California Institute of
the Arts where animation greats such as John

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:51.110
Lasseter and Brad Bird studied.
Hank from Pixar's upcoming movie Finding Dory

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:55.579
appears in the rock pool that Arlo falls into
after being bitten by a gopher.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:59.520
You'll need to watch it very carefully as
when Arlo first falls in, the octopus's eyes

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.260
are closed.
By the way, in Finding Dory, Hank will be

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:07.930
voiced by Modern Family star Ed O'Neill.
There's a clever nod to Monsters University

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.710
character "Squishy" during the hilarious hallucination
that Arlo and Spot have after they eat some

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:16.250
rotten fruit.
Arlo and Spot float through the air, swap

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:21.010
heads and the five eyes which appear on Arlo
are a reference to Scott "Squishy" Squibbles

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.600
who was actually voiced by The Good Dinosaur
director Peter Sohn!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.210
And you'll need eagle eyes to see this one
but during that same hallucination scene,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:35.049
the Luxo ball actually floats by.
The Luxo ball originates from Pixar's very

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:40.340
first animation, a short film called Luxo
Jr, which features both the Luxo ball and

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.740
the two desk lamps, one of which appear in
Pixar's logo.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.130
By the way, the hallucination scene also has
shades of when Dumbo and Timothy Q Mouse got

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:54.310
drunk on champagne, and started hallucinating
pink and multi-coloured elephants.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.570
And Spot might be an ancestor of Finding Nemo's
Darla.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:03.159
They both have a very similar shaped face
and eyes, freckles and a snub nose.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:07.170
In Finding Nemo, Darla is called a fish killer
by other fish and interestingly the first

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.180
name that Forrest Woodbush, the Pet Collector,
comes up with for Spot is "Killer".

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:17.189
And in that naming scene when Forrest Woodbush
and Arlo compete to see who gets to keep Spot,

00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:20.150
there are a whole bunch of shout-outs to other
Pixar characters.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:25.980
There's Squirt, the playful turtle from Finding
Nemo, Frank the combine harvester from Cars,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:32.540
Stinky Pete the Prospector from Toy Story
2, Violet, the daughter of Bob and Helen Parr

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.739
in The Incredibles, and Spike which is the
alter-ego for the slug-like employee Augustus

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:41.739
Jones at Monsters, Inc!
Oh, and by the way, Spike was also the real

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:46.999
name of the dog who played Old Yeller in the
classic 1957 Disney movie, which director

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:51.909
Peter Sohn has said was a big influence on
The Good Dinosaur.

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:55.959
When Arlo and Spot are running away from a
bunch of pterodactyls, they see what looks

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.260
like the silhouette of an adult Apatosaurus
in the distance, an easter egg for the Dinoco

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.930
sign in Toy Story, although as they get closer
they see the silhouette is actually made up

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:10.199
of two T-rexes.
And finally, this one was perhaps the toughest

00:03:10.199 --> 00:03:14.620
to spot, but floating out here at the very
start of the film in the asteroid belt is

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.629
the Pizza Planet Truck itself!
The Pizza Planet Truck first appeared in Toy

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:23.739
Story and has made an appearance in every
Pixar feature film since then except The Incredibles.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:28.089
So, guys which other easter eggs did you spot
in The Good Dinosaur? And do tell me which

00:03:28.089 --> 00:03:32.339
is your favourite Pixar movie?!
If you enjoyed this video, I'll have another

00:03:32.339 --> 00:03:37.129
easter egg video coming shortly for Disney's
Zootopia and you might also like to check

00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:42.089
out these 25 awesome behind-the-scenes facts
about the making of Pixar's Inside Out.

00:03:42.089 --> 00:03:47.559
As always, your likes, comments and shares
are hugely appreciated; and do please subscribe

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:51.939
if you want to see more videos like this.
Thanks for watching and see you next time.

00:03:51.939 --> 00:03:53.290
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

